# The repo's canonical text form is LF, enforced at checkout too: no smudge
# boundary between working tree and repo, so byte-level gates (verify-*
# comparisons, blob hashing, coverage offsets) see one form on every host.
# If a file class ever genuinely needs CRLF in the working tree (.bat/.cmd
# for cmd.exe), add a `*.bat text eol=crlf` override AFTER this line — the
# in-repo form stays LF; CRLF becomes checkout-time presentation only.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.pdf binary
# Pairing records are generated from the three confirmed owner-blob pairs.
# The worktree-local installer registers the fail-closed driver command.
*.i18n.yaml merge=dsh-translation-pairing
project-plan/**/*.bundle filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# A run package is evidence, and its manifest's SHA-256 is over these bytes. The working tree has
# to keep them exactly as the run wrote them — trailing spaces included, since the tables the run
# produces are column-aligned — and no line-ending conversion may sit between the file on disk and
# the digest beside it. Without this, `git diff --check` demanded a trim that would have invalidated
# every digest in the manifest: the delivered package lost twenty bytes that way, and could no
# longer be verified against the manifest it came with.
project-plan/**/package-*/** -text -whitespace
